  "notes": "The Bay entry that is *played* rather than programmed: E-A-Ski and CMT's documented 90s method used live music and instrumentation rather than sampling, so the harmony can genuinely modulate within a song — which is why this is the only entry in this batch whose chord set reaches four chords with a borrowed dominant and a v→i turn, and why `extensions` is minor-7th/9th heavy at 0.52 combined. \"Mordant, bass-driven funk\" is a bass instruction, and it is authored as one: `followRootsProb` 0.35 with the widest passing-tone set here including the major 7th, a 21-semitone register and continuous motion, against Celly Cel's static sub in the same city. His vocal habit — half-sung sing-song delivery with rapid triplet subdivisions — is the primary parameter and has no generator, so what carries it is a melody with a high step share and a long 4-bar phrase, the closest a note line gets to a sung one. ⚠ `medium` on the research's medium-high. INFERRED: the borrowed `V` weight and the 4-bar cycle length, which follow from \"harmony is played and can modulate\" rather than from a named progression. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 49 to 47 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 48 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 2.",
